---
import Aurora from '../../components/Aurora.astro';
import Specimen from '../Specimen.astro';
---
<Specimen title="Principles" surface="none">
    <div class="principles">
        <p><strong>CSS only.</strong> Every effect is declarative CSS; nothing depends on JavaScript to appear.</p>
        <p><strong>Subtle.</strong> Motion explains structure or adds atmosphere. It never blocks reading.</p>
        <p><strong>Optional.</strong> Under <code>prefers-reduced-motion</code>, everything is static and fully visible.</p>
        <p><strong>Progressive.</strong> Scroll-driven effects run where the browser supports them; elsewhere the content is simply there.</p>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Headline slide-up" code={'<h1><span class="mask-line"><span>Line one</span></span>…</h1>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>On page load, each line rises out of its own mask, staggered by 120ms. Reload the page to replay it.</p></Fragment>
    <p class="demo-headline" role="presentation">
        <span class="mask-line"><span>Each line rises</span></span>
        <span class="mask-line"><span class="gradient-text">out of its mask.</span></span>
    </p>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Entrance" code={'<p class="rise rise-2">…</p>  /* rise-2, rise-3, rise-4 add a stagger */'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Supporting copy and buttons fade up on load, a beat after the headline.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="cluster">
        <span class="chip-demo rise">rise</span>
        <span class="chip-demo rise rise-2">rise-2</span>
        <span class="chip-demo rise rise-3">rise-3</span>
        <span class="chip-demo rise rise-4">rise-4</span>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Scroll reveals" code={'<div class="reveal">…</div>        /* slides up as it enters the viewport */\n<div class="reveal-scale">…</div>  /* tiles grow into place */\n<img class="settle" … />           /* product shots settle into frame */'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Driven by the scroll position, not timers. Text moves but never fades, so it keeps full contrast throughout.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="grid grid-3">
        <div class="tile demo-tile reveal">reveal</div>
        <div class="tile demo-tile reveal-scale">reveal-scale</div>
        <div class="tile demo-tile settle">settle</div>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Aurora" padding="none" code={'<Aurora palette="brand" />  /* brand | aero | studio | player */'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Brand light drifting slowly behind a hero, in both themes. Each capstone product has its own palette.</p></Fragment>
    <div class="aurora-demo">
        <Aurora />
        <p class="label">Aurora · brand</p>
    </div>
    <div class="aurora-row">
        <div class="aurora-demo small"><Aurora palette="aero" /><p class="label">aero</p></div>
        <div class="aurora-demo small"><Aurora palette="studio" /><p class="label">studio</p></div>
        <div class="aurora-demo small"><Aurora palette="player" /><p class="label">player</p></div>
    </div>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Gradient shimmer" code={'<span class="gradient-text">…</span>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>Gradient phrases drift slowly through the spectrum.</p></Fragment>
    <p class="demo-headline"><span class="gradient-text">A slow shimmer.</span></p>
</Specimen>

<Specimen title="Scroll progress" code={'<div class="header-progress scroll-progress" aria-hidden="true"></div>'}>
    <Fragment slot="notes"><p>The continuous brand spectrum along the bottom of the header, painted at full width and revealed from left to right as the page scrolls, so more colour appears rather than the bar stretching. Scroll this page to see it.</p></Fragment>
    <p class="muted">Look at the bottom edge of the site header.</p>
</Specimen>

<style>
    .principles {
        display: grid;
        gap: 0.75rem;
        max-width: 44rem;
    }

    .demo-headline {
        color: var(--heading);
        font-family: var(--font-display);
        font-size: var(--text-5xl);
        font-weight: 600;
        letter-spacing: -0.04em;
        line-height: 1.04;
    }

    .chip-demo {
        padding: 0.6rem 1rem;
        border-radius: 999px;
        background: var(--bg-alt);
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: var(--text-xs);
    }

    .demo-tile {
        display: grid;
        place-items: center;
        height: 10rem;
        box-shadow: var(--shadow-tile);
        font-family: var(--font-mono);
        font-size: var(--text-sm);
    }

    .aurora-demo {
        position: relative;
        display: grid;
        place-items: end start;
        height: 18rem;
        padding: 1.5rem;
        border: 1px solid var(--border);
        border-radius: var(--radius-lg);
        background: var(--bg);
        isolation: isolate;
        overflow: hidden;
    }

    .aurora-demo :global(.aurora) {
        -webkit-mask-image: none;
        mask-image: none;
    }

    .aurora-row {
        display: grid;
        gap: var(--tile-gap);
        margin-top: var(--tile-gap);
    }

    @media (min-width: 48rem) {
        .aurora-row {
            grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
        }
    }

    .aurora-demo.small {
        height: 12rem;
    }
</style>
